<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Baltic Ballet, 2019</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Overview&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;2017 was a rocky year for Vladimar Putin. His prized naval base in Syria withered due to lack of oil and gas revenue. Russians had to withstand a series of terrorist strikes in Syria and the Republic of Georgia. Barely winning reelection in 2018, Putin needed a&amp;nbsp;WIN somewhere.&amp;nbsp;During 2017, NATO steadily reinforced ground troops along the border with Russia.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Kaliningrad had several readiness exercises in the Fall of 2018. In response, the Baltic states partially mobilized. To the world's surprise, a new organization called the Gotland Independence Front made its appearance on the internet on&amp;nbsp;New Year's Day 2019.&amp;nbsp;Their wed page stated that the movement&amp;nbsp;formed because of Sweden's unwillingness to exploit energy deposits just off their shore to the benefit the Islanders. On February 12, the Gotland Independence Front claimed to&amp;nbsp;have&amp;nbsp;seized control of these resources and formed separate government - all comminication to the island was cut at midnight and the entire island went dark. &lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 17px; FONT-FAMILY: 'Duplicate Ionic Regular'; WHITE-SPACE: normal; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; WORD-SPACING: 0px; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;SAPO's Director General Anders Thornberg told reporters on that one person has been arrested "in absentia" for plotting attacks and that the plans weren't directly related to ongoing events. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 17px; FONT-FAMILY: knowledge-reg, helvetica, arial, sans-serif; WHITE-SPACE: normal; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; WORD-SPACING: 0px; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: rgb(17,17,17); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;A spokesman for the military declined to give any more details.&lt;/FONT&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;On the morning of February 13, Olso held a crisis meeting and decided it&amp;nbsp;was prudent to step up air and sea patrols around Gotland to feel out the situation. Is the Gotland Independence Front for real?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;See: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;A href="https://disciplescientist.wordpress.com/2015/03/04/what-if-russia-demands-a-naval-base-in-finland/"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;https://disciplescientist.wordpress.com/2015/03/04/what-if-russia-demands-a-naval-base-in-finland/&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;Kevin Kinscherf&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoPlainText style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;A href="mailto:kevinkin@comcast.net"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;kevinkin@comcast.net&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
